{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"restorePurchases","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxPaywall\/EntitlementSnapshot","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SwiduxPaywall19EntitlementSnapshotV","text":"EntitlementSnapshot","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A restore is a write: its result is the account’s state as of its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"completion, newer than any read that resolved while it ran — even one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that started later. So it is persisted like a stream event, superseding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every read still in flight, rather than ordered by when it started.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two things outrank it: a base-stream event persisted after the restore","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"began (the provider’s feed is at least as new), and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPaywall\/documentation\/SwiduxPaywall\/ResilientPaywallService\/clearCache()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(the restore began for an account the app has since signed out of).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Either way it returns what the cache now holds, as a superseded read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does, or throws if nothing usable is cached.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"role":"symbo